WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.657
Now you will build the cleaning and EDA workflow yourself.

00:00:03.657 --> 00:00:07.992
Start with the provided messy dataset.

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:10.342
First audit it.

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:15.652
Then remove the confirmed duplicate, convert date and amount safely, standardize region and channel labels,

00:00:15.652 --> 00:00:23.406
and flag invalid values. After that, create a missing-value report and summarize amount by region.

00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:27.189
Do not try to write the entire solution at once.

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:33.059
Complete one step, run it, inspect the result, and then continue.

00:00:33.059 --> 00:00:39.794
That approach makes debugging easier and helps you understand what each transformation changes.

00:00:39.794 --> 00:00:45.604
At the end, write two or three sentences about what you found during EDA.

00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:49.059
The goal is not only to produce a cleaned table.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:56.585
The goal is to explain the quality problems, the decisions you made, and the patterns you observed after cleaning.
